course: dictionary
lesson: 15458
title: Stimulation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stimulation is a noun. It comes from the verb stimulate, which means to make something more active. Stimulation can be the action itself, or the thing that does it. «Children need play and stimulation to keep their minds growing.» Here, stimulation means things that keep the mind busy and interested.
explain: Stimulation can also be about the body. In science, a nerve, a sense or a cell is stimulated when something makes it react, such as light, sound, touch or electricity. «The scientist used electrical stimulation to make the muscle react.» Here, electrical stimulation means using electricity to cause a reaction.
explain: Too much stimulation can be a problem. «The room was full of loud noise, flashing lights and screens, and Sam felt tired and upset.» This is overstimulation: more stimulation than a person can comfortably handle. Look at the words around stimulation to work out which meaning fits.
fact: Stimulation is a noun: the action of stimulating, or the thing that stimulates.
fact: «Stimulation» can mean making something more active, or something that keeps the mind busy and interested.
fact: In biology, stimulation is when a nerve, sense or cell is made to react, for example by light, sound, touch or electricity.
fact: «Mental stimulation» means activities that keep the mind busy and interested.
fact: «Overstimulation» means too much stimulation, which can make people tired or upset.
exercise: «Children need play and stimulation to learn.» What does stimulation mean here? | Heavy, cold weather | *Things that keep the mind busy and interested | A type of deep sleep | Being very quiet and still
exercise: In science, what does stimulation of a nerve mean? | When a nerve stops working for ever | When a nerve is cut in two | When a nerve is covered in cream | *When a nerve is made to react, for example by light or touch
exercise: «The noise and flashing lights left Ava tired and upset.» What is this called? | *Too much stimulation | Overstimulation | Relaxation | Hibernation
test: A scientist uses electricity to make a muscle react. What is this? | *Electrical stimulation | Overstimulation | Mental stimulation | Lack of stimulation
test: Which word is the noun, not the verb? | Stimulate | Stimulating | *Stimulation
exam: Which sentence uses stimulation correctly? | The rain stopped and the sun came out. | Tom ate his lunch very quickly. | *Puzzles and books give the mind good stimulation. | The dog slept all afternoon by the fire.
